WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.660
TV land sure isn't the cozy safe haven it
used to be.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:09.500
In recent years, dedicated viewers have lost
beloved characters on everything from Game

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.090
of Thrones to Stranger Things to even Will
and Grace.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:18.370
So far, it looks like 2018 is shaping up to
be another small-screen bloodbath.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:23.050
Get the tissues ready, because we're looking
back at a few characters who've unexpectedly

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:27.670
left us in 2018 - but be careful if you're
not caught up on these shows, because this

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:28.670
one's loaded with …

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:29.800
"Spoilers."

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:33.160
Carl - The Walking Dead

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:37.829
Carl Grimes - and actor Chandler Riggs, for
that matter - grew up on TV.

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:42.949
The son of Walking Dead protagonist Rick Grimes,
he'd been with the series since it started

00:00:42.949 --> 00:00:44.320
in 2010.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.889
Along the way, he endured tragedies and setbacks,
including the loss of his mother during childbirth,

00:00:49.889 --> 00:00:55.449
the loss of an eye, and various acts of evil
by villains like the Governor and Negan.

00:00:55.449 --> 00:01:00.670
Keeping Carl alive and safe was the reason
Rick never completely crumbled, and Carl kept

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:04.720
human decency alive 'til the end - which is
what ultimately killed him.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.300
"Carl's dead."

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:17.710
Carl left Alexandria to help the mysterious
Siddiq mercy-kill zombies because Siddiq believed

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.390
it freed their souls.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:23.109
Turned out one of those zombies took a bite
out of Carl - as zombies do.

00:01:23.109 --> 00:01:29.000
It was a death sentence, but not an immediate
one, giving Carl enough time to say goodbye.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.870
He hung out with his little sister Judith,
wrote devastating farewell letters to Enid,

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:38.969
Michonne, and Rick, and then - so his end
could be on his own terms - he shot himself

00:01:38.969 --> 00:01:42.539
offscreen before he could go full walker.

00:01:42.539 --> 00:01:44.649
Tobin - The Walking Dead

00:01:44.649 --> 00:01:49.619
Fans have always had mixed feelings about
Tobin, a resident of Alexandria who first

00:01:49.619 --> 00:01:51.479
showed up in Season 5.

00:01:51.479 --> 00:01:55.820
On the one hand, his relationship with Carol
was interesting, but on the other hand, he

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:00.579
just up and abandoned Francine to a zombie
attack in order to save his own skin.

00:02:00.579 --> 00:02:04.490
Well, fans no longer have to feel conflicted
about Tobin, because he's dead.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:09.660
Thanks to an infected stab wound, Tobin turned
into a zombie and killed several of his former

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.720
allies before being put down for good by Carol.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.240
Talk about a bad way to go out!

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:17.580
Simon - The Walking Dead

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:22.710
There's an old saying among Walking Dead fans:
lie down with zombie dogs, you get zombie

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:23.710
fleas.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.410
Simon found that out the hard way.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:29.930
As the second in command to the Walking Dead's
cartoonishly evil Negan, it was only a matter

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:33.720
of time before he found himself staring down
Lucille's business end.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:37.940
And sure enough, Negan finally got tired of
Simon plotting behind his back, leading to

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:42.630
a one-on-one showdown that ultimately ended
with Simon's zombified corpse being strung

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:43.760
up as a warning.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.000
Yikes!

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:48.440
Nick Clark - Fear the Walking Dead

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:53.250
Fear the Walking Dead has always played second
fiddle to its parent show, The Walking Dead.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:58.160
So in season four, AMC attempted to fix that
by bringing in a bunch of new faces, along

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:01.070
with classic Walking Dead character Morgan.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:03.670
All those additions meant there had to be
some subtractions.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:08.130
And the most shocking was the loss of Frank
Dillane's Nick Clark, who was at the center

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:11.480
of many of the show's storylines over the
first three seasons.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:15.110
Dillane had reportedly asked to be written
off the series, though, making it an easy

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:19.840
choice for producers, who disposed of Clark
by having Charlie, a tween working as a mole

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.150
for a different survival group, shoot him
dead.

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:27.690
Cigarette Smoking Man, Skinner, and Reyes
- The X-Files

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:33.840
Love it or hate it, one thing's for certain:
The X-Files' season 11 finale aimed to shock.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:39.430
One of the season's main arcs concerned Cigarette
Smoking Man's plans to unleash a lethal virus

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:44.931
on the world, and to pull it off, he'd manipulated
Scully's shape-shifting son William, along

00:03:44.931 --> 00:03:50.650
with FBI Assistant Director Walter Skinner
and Agent Monica Reyes, into helping him execute

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:51.650
it.

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:56.780
CSM - portrayed with ominous perfection by
William B. Davis - also happened to be William's

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.230
biological father.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:03.990
Yup, he was the one who'd drugged and medically
impregnated Scully nearly two decades ago.

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:09.980
William, wishing to be free of all this evil
awfulness, finally confronted CSM on a dock

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:13.060
while using his powers to disguise himself
as Mulder.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:16.280
CSM then shot William-as-Mulder in the head.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:22.370
Then the real Mulder, distraught and devastated,
shot CSM a bunch of times and shoved him into

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:23.370
the water.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:28.400
This means that one of the series' biggest
and most memorable big bads is finally gone.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:32.910
However, he caused some collateral damage
on the way: Earlier in the episode, after

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:38.610
Skinner shot one-time Scully replacement Agent
Monica Reyes, the FBI Assistant Director was

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:42.310
apparently run over with a car driven by CSM.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:43.310
Maybe.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:46.680
Honestly, is anybody ever really deceased
on The X-Files?

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:50.870
Even William burst out of the water at the
end of the episode, so who knows for sure?

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:53.720
"Everyone still dies in the end."

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.680
Ferguson - New Girl

00:04:55.680 --> 00:05:00.600
Fox's New Girl isn't so new anymore, and it's
come to the end of its seven-season run with

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:05.500
a handful of episodes that wrapped up all
of its loose ends and gave each of its characters

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:06.810
a proper send-off.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:11.460
Nick and Jess have finally gotten together
for good, Schmidt and CeCe have a young daughter

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:16.510
named Ruth, Winston and an extremely pregnant
Aly are expecting … and, at some point during

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:19.760
the three-year time jump between seasons,
someone passed away.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.880
"Ferguson died of a heart attack."

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:22.880
"What?"

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.970
"Yes, the coroner said nothing about glitter."

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.340
"Did you say coroner?"

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:31.250
That would be Ferguson, the beloved smush-faced
cat belonging to Winston.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:35.160
Winston acquired Ferguson back in season two
- she belonged to a girlfriend, and when she

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:38.450
cheated on him, he found peace by adopting
the cat.

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:43.610
While viewers were spared the not-very-sitcom-friendly
images and emotional turmoil of watching a

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:49.139
pet pass away, New Girl devoted an episode
to Winston's over-the-top grieving process,

00:05:49.139 --> 00:05:54.470
which involves a motorcade to an elaborate
memorial service conducted in the Jewish tradition.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:56.460
Spencer - American Housewife

00:05:56.460 --> 00:06:02.900
A relatable family sitcom injected with a
hefty dose of social satire, ABC's American

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:07.780
Housewife concerns a middle-class family trying
to keep their values and decency in check

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:11.280
while living in the ultra-rich and superficial
town of Westport, Connecticut.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:16.400
The middle child Oliver is determined to be
as rich as his peers someday.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:21.350
Part of that involved befriending a new neighbor,
a disgraced Wolf of Wall Street type just

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:24.430
released from prison named Spencer, played
by George Hamilton.

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:29.290
While Oliver initially intended to just be
nice to get in the old guy's will, a true

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:32.730
friendship and grandfather/grandson relationship
developed.

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:37.130
He kept Oliver in check against the greed
of the community, which is why it was so shocking

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:41.890
that American Housewife writers had him pass
away late in the second season.

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:43.950
Clayton Reeves - NCIS

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:50.400
NCIS wound down its 15th season with a heavily
promoted plot: The departure of original character

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:55.530
Abby, whose longtime portrayer, actress Pauley
Perrette, was ready to move on.

00:06:55.530 --> 00:07:00.620
NCIS fans suspected that Abby might be written
off the show the way characters are most commonly

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:04.510
and effectively removed from a series: by
putting them 6 feet under.

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:09.139
It certainly appeared that this fate had befallen
lab tech Abby, especially since in what was

00:07:09.139 --> 00:07:13.949
Perrette's second-to-last episode, she and
co-worker Clayton Reeves struggled over a

00:07:13.949 --> 00:07:15.361
gun with a yet-to-be-identified assailant.

00:07:15.361 --> 00:07:19.389
Then, a gunshot rang out as the screen cut
to black.

00:07:19.389 --> 00:07:24.830
The following episode depicted Ducky sympathizing
with another coroner about the agony of performing

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:27.180
an autopsy on a former colleague.

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:30.710
And then, as the body bag is unzipped, Reeves
is shown inside.

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:34.870
Evidently, he'd selflessly stepped in front
of Abby to take the bullet.

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:39.220
As for Abby, she was in the hospital, but
she pulled through, and played an integral

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:43.990
role in one last high-stakes NCIS adventure.

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:46.011
Artie Goodman - Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt

00:07:46.011 --> 00:07:52.199
At the end of season three, Unbreakable Kimmy
Schmidt's resident grump, Lillian, had unexpectedly

00:07:52.199 --> 00:07:57.250
found true love with Artie Goodman, her rival
in a battle over neighborhood gentrification.

00:07:57.250 --> 00:08:01.229
But at the start of season four, fans got
a surprise when it was revealed that Artie

00:08:01.229 --> 00:08:06.070
had unexpectedly died, leaving Lillian in
charge of disposing of his ashes.

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:10.460
She eventually did it in her own signature
fashion, selling two plastic baggies of his

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:15.710
remains for $1,200 to some folks who clearly
thought those ashes were something a little

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:18.050
more party-friendly.

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:20.479
Butch and R'as al Ghul - Gotham

00:08:20.479 --> 00:08:25.270
Deaths on Gotham are frequent, but they're
usually just underlings, stooges, or random

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:27.600
victims of the future Rogue's Gallery.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:31.490
In the season four finale, though, two major
bad guys bit the dust.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:36.959
Bruce, aka the former Solomon Grundy, was
executed by the Penguin, though being an immortal

00:08:36.959 --> 00:08:39.830
swamp monster might reverse that in future
seasons.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:44.099
Meanwhile, Ra's al Ghul was stabbed to death
by Barbara, with a little help from the only

00:08:44.099 --> 00:08:46.360
person who can kill him for good, Bruce Wayne.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:51.380
Of course, Ra's also has a habit of returning
from the dead thanks to his Lazarus Pit, but

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:55.649
for now, he's among this year's list of shocking
casualties.

00:08:55.649 --> 00:08:57.889
Will Simpson - Jessica Jones

00:08:57.889 --> 00:09:02.930
In the first season of Jessica Jones, good
guy cop Will Simpson turned out to actually

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:07.660
be a total creeper with a dark and mysterious
past that involved government experiments

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:08.730
gone wrong.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:12.439
It seemed he was being set up to become the
comic book anti-hero Nuke.

00:09:12.439 --> 00:09:15.399
That expectation was confounded in season
two, though.

00:09:15.399 --> 00:09:19.779
Yes, he was totally stalking Trish, but after
she confronted him, it turned out he was trying

00:09:19.779 --> 00:09:24.930
to warn her about someone even more dangerous
- a someone who then promptly snapped his

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:25.930
neck.

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:27.790
So much for that subplot!

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:29.389
Jack - This Is Us

00:09:29.389 --> 00:09:34.839
Due to the show's non-linear, flashback-heavy
structure, the millions of rabid fans of NBC's

00:09:34.839 --> 00:09:41.100
smash hit tearjerker This Is Us knew that
Pearson patriarch Jack - played by Milo Ventimiglia

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:44.490
- was going to die, but they weren't quite
sure how.

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:50.040
This Is Us used its post-Super Bowl time slot
to deliver a very special episode on February

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:53.240
4th, revealing exactly what led to Pearson's
passing.

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:58.730
The previous episode ended with a flashback
sequence set in 1998, showing the family's

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:04.350
slow cooker short out and spark a massive
fire that quickly engulfs the Pearson home.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:08.899
Jack wakes up in the middle of the night and
turns into Hero Dad, getting his family out

00:10:08.899 --> 00:10:10.879
of the house with a bedsheet rope.

00:10:10.879 --> 00:10:14.220
His wife Rebecca takes him to the hospital
to attend to his minor burns.

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:18.640
Then she steps out of the room for just a
second… long enough for an ER doctor to

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:23.029
tell her that Jack passed away of cardiac
arrest brought on by smoke inhalation.

00:10:23.029 --> 00:10:25.910
"Your husband went into cardiac arrest.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:29.879
It was catastrophic and…

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:32.620
I-I'm afraid we've lost him."

00:10:33.769 --> 00:10:35.160
We're not ugly crying!

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.339
You're ugly crying!

00:10:37.339 --> 00:10:38.459
Thanks for watching!

00:10:38.459 --> 00:10:41.490
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:44.249
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

